-- title:
--   Free factors and algebraic extensions of subgroups of F_d (Puder §3.1)
-- statement:
--   Definitions for subgroups of the free group $\mathbf F_d$ (`FreeGroup (Fin d)`) on $g_1, \dots, g_d$, from Puder's §3.1.
--
--   - `Puder.IsFreeFactor H J`: $H$ is a *free factor* of $J$, that is, $H$ is the subgroup generated by a subset $S$ of some basis $b$ of $J$ (a `FreeGroupBasis` of $J$ indexed by some type). Then $b$ restricted to $S$ is a basis of $H$ that extends to the basis $b$ of $J$, which is Puder's definition. Puder, p. 12, footnote: “If $H \le J$ are free groups then $H$ is said to be a *free factor* of $J$ if a (every) basis of $H$ can be extended to a basis of $J$.” The definition takes the “a” reading; the “(every)” in the footnote is a known consequence, not part of the definition.
--   - `Puder.IsAlgExt H J`: $J$ is an *algebraic extension* of $H$, written $H \le_{alg} J$: $H \le J$ and no subgroup $L$ with $H \le L < J$ is a free factor of $J$. Puder, p. 12: “Let $H \le J$ be subgroups of $\mathbf F_k$. We say that $J$ is an *algebraic extension* of $H$ and denote $H \le_{alg} J$, if there is *no* intermediate subgroup $H \le L \lneq J$ which is a proper free factor of $J$.” A free factor $L$ of $J$ with $L \lneq J$ is what “proper free factor” means. Puder writes $H \lneq_{alg} J$ for $H \le_{alg} J$ with $H \ne J$; statements write that as `IsAlgExt H J ∧ H ≠ J`.
--
--   Source: D. Puder, *Expansion of random graphs: new proofs, new results*, Invent. Math. 201 (2015) 845–908, https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-014-0560-x (arXiv:1212.5216, §3.1, p. 12).
-- source:
--   Puder, D., Expansion of random graphs: new proofs, new results, Invent. Math. 201 (2015) 845–908, https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-014-0560-x (arXiv:1212.5216), p. 12, §3.1, free factors and algebraic extensions

import Mathlib

/-!
# Free factors and algebraic extensions of subgroups of a free group (Puder)

Puder, *Expansion of random graphs: new proofs, new results*, Invent. Math. 201 (2015),
§3.1 (arXiv:1212.5216, p. 12).
-/

namespace Puder

/-- Puder p. 12, footnote: `H` is a free factor of `J`: `H` is generated by a subset of
some basis of `J`. -/
def IsFreeFactor {d : ℕ} (H J : Subgroup (FreeGroup (Fin d))) : Prop :=
  ∃ (ι : Type) (b : FreeGroupBasis ι J) (S : Set ι),
    H = Subgroup.closure ((fun i => (b i : FreeGroup (Fin d))) '' S)

/-- Puder p. 12: `J` is an algebraic extension of `H` (`H ≤_alg J`): `H ≤ J` and no subgroup
`L` with `H ≤ L < J` is a free factor of `J`. -/
def IsAlgExt {d : ℕ} (H J : Subgroup (FreeGroup (Fin d))) : Prop :=
  H ≤ J ∧ ∀ L : Subgroup (FreeGroup (Fin d)), H ≤ L → L < J → ¬ IsFreeFactor L J

end Puder


